        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "In the given $x$-order,\n\n$\\dfrac{2}{x-2}$ gives $-\\dfrac13,-\\dfrac25,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac23,-1,-2,*,2,1$.\n\n$-\\dfrac{2}{x+2}$ gives $1,2,*,-2,-1,-\\dfrac23,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac25,-\\dfrac13$.",
          "worked": "Substitute each header value into each function. For example, at $x=-4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{-4-2}&=-\\frac13\\\\-\\frac{2}{-4+2}&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe denominator is zero at $x=2$ for the first function and at $x=-2$ for the second, so those entries are undefined. The completed second row reverses the order of the first row because the graphs are reflections in the $y$-axis.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
